@startuml back-to-back
' Back-to-back transactions inside a burst (docs/spec/02-line-conditions.md, section 2.4).
' CLK stays high from STOP to the next START, so no pending slave can announce itself in between.
' Only after the final STOP does CLK fall, and a slave that is still pending signals at that edge.
scale 10 as 90 pixels
hide time-axis
binary "CLK" as CLK
binary "DATA" as DATA
concise "Bus" as P
concise "Pending slave" as S

@0
CLK is low
DATA is high
P is "transaction n"
S is {-}
@10
CLK is high
@20
CLK is low
@22
DATA is low
@30
CLK is high
P is "STOP + START"
@35
DATA is high
@40
DATA is low
@45
CLK is low
P is "transaction n+1"
@48
DATA is high
@55
CLK is high
@65
CLK is low
@68
DATA is low
@75
CLK is high
P is "final STOP"
@80
DATA is high
@90
CLK is low
P is idle
@92
DATA is low
S is "announces itself"
@110
P is {-}
S is {-}

highlight 30 to 45 #LightBlue : CLK stays high
@enduml
